-- title:
--   Evaluation sequence along a thickened invertible ideal sheaf
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme and let $\mathcal I$ be an ideal sheaf datum on $X$ which is invertible in the sense that every point of $X$ lies in some basic open $X_f$, for $f$ a section over an affine open $U$, such that the ideal cut out by $\mathcal I$ on the affine basic open determined by $f$ is generated by a single non-zerodivisor. Let $L$ be a module on $X$ which is invertible in the sense that every point has an open neighbourhood $V$ over which the pullback of $L$ along $V \hookrightarrow X$ is isomorphic to the unit sheaf of modules, and let $r,n,d$ be natural numbers with $d + n = r$. For an ideal sheaf datum $\mathcal J$ write $\mathcal J^{\vee}$ for the dual of the kernel of the canonical map from the unit to the pushforward of the unit along the closed immersion $\mathcal J$ defines. Then, writing $\eta$ for the unit of the pullback–pushforward adjunction attached to the closed immersion of the subscheme defined by $\mathcal I^{n}$, evaluated at $L \otimes (\mathcal I^{r})^{\vee}$, the assertion is twofold: $\eta$ is an epimorphism, and there exists a morphism $\iota : L \otimes (\mathcal I^{d})^{\vee} \to L \otimes (\mathcal I^{r})^{\vee}$ together with a proof that $\iota$ followed by $\eta$ is zero, such that the resulting short complex $L \otimes (\mathcal I^{d})^{\vee} \to L \otimes (\mathcal I^{r})^{\vee} \to \eta$'s target is short exact.
--
--   This is the ideal-sheaf sequence of the $n$-th thickening $nD$ of the effective Cartier divisor $D$ cut out by $\mathcal I$, twisted by the invertible module $L \otimes \mathcal O(rD)$, in the form $0 \to L(dD) \to L(rD) \to L(rD)|_{nD} \to 0$ with $d+n=r$; the quotient map is recorded as the adjunction unit itself rather than as an abstract epimorphism, so that its direct images along a relative curve are literally the evaluation maps. It is used in the construction of the relative Picard functor, for local freeness and determinant statements for pushforwards along thickenings, for the short exactness of those pushed-forward sequences, and in the production of sections of twists of powers of $\mathcal I$ over a smooth proper curve.
